 "last_rtl_message": {
  "stage": "rtl-design-creation",
  "visit": 1,
  "text": "The RTL is written and passes lint and simulation, but the V3 gate still fails. I did not fix the remaining V3 items because they sit in the testplan and the bench, not in the RTL.\n\n**Written:** `rtl/crc32_core.sv`, `rtl/crc32_top.sv`, `rtl/reset_gen.sv`, `rtl/xilinx_sim_stubs.sv` and `build.yaml`.\n\n**Passing:**\n- Lint passes.\n- The Verilator simulation passes on seeds 1\u20133, and V0, V1 and V2 pass.\n- Line coverage is 100%.\n- All cover properties are hit.\n- The `check` run at RTL scope shows no failures (resets and methodology were not run at this scope).\n\n**Still failing at V3:**\n- **Functional bins:** none are planned. `verif/testplan.yaml` needs `bins:` names, and the bench has to export `coverage_func.yml`.\n- **Toggle coverage:** it is 62%, against the 80% threshold. The gaps are mostly constant bits: `rpoly`, `sfp_tx_disable`, the stubbed `build_word` and the constant `DESIGN_ID` bits. These need waivers with reasons in the testplan.\n- **Evidence the flow produces later:**\n  - mutation score\n  - CDC structure and CDC injection results\n  - post-synthesis analysis results\n  - hardware bring-up results\n\n**Assumptions to check:**\n- **Device:** the top uses `MMCME4_BASE`, which I chose for the xck26 (UltraScale+) in the spec. The task text quoted an `xc7a100t` part. I wrote `build.yaml` with the xck26 part, and the part is not verified against the board's actual build.\n- **Constraints:** I left `design.xdc` as `board_constraints` wrote it. Its `set_output_delay` on the LEDs is referenced to the 25 MHz pin clock, while those outputs are launched from the 125 MHz clock. Post-synthesis timing may flag that, and I did not check it.\n\nDONE"
 },
